# ── Regenerable / large: never commit ──────────────────────────────────────
# These are derived from the HF corpora and the training run. Between them they
# are ~530 MB, which is why they are ignored rather than tracked.
data/
datasets/
reports/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# Model checkpoints and training ballots: every run writes a new best.pt plus
# two ballots. Together these are ~130 MB per run and are fully regenerable
# from data/ + datasets/, so only the small run reports are worth keeping.
experiments/*/best.pt
experiments/*/*.jsonl
checkpoints/

# ── Committed on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v2/runtime/ holds the model the server actually loads (server/ml/v2Bridge.js
# requires ../../v2/runtime/onnx_classifier). At ~3 MB it is cheap to track, and
# committing it means a fresh clone or a Render build boots with a working model
# and needs neither the Python/GPU pipeline nor a network fetch.
#
# The same artifact is published at huggingface.co/dr0wzy/aizen-siem/runtimev2,
# and server/services/datasetDownloader.js re-fetches it if it is missing, so
# deleting these locally is safe -- the server just downloads them at boot.
#
# v2/eval/baseline.json is committed too: it is the reference check:model
# compares against, and without it the gate degrades to a 25% sanity bar.

# Local venvs and installed packages, not source.
runtime/fastapi/
runtime/node_modules/
*.onnx.tmp
